We have web-scrapped the semi-structured Financial Statements (FS) - mainly Balance Sheets (BS), Income Statements (IS) and Cash-flow Statements (CS) - of 2292 listed Indian companies for five years (2010 to 2014)666https://www.moneycontrol.com/. We extracted a total of 42 financial variables - or just variables - (28 from BS, 9 from IS and 5 from CS) and 22 financial ratios, which we used to find companies with misinformation in their FS. Tables LABEL:tab:var\_stat\_2014, [5](https://arxiv.org/html/2607.17797v1#S4.T5 "Table 5 ‣ 4 Unsupervised Methods for Misinformation Detection ‣ Financial Audit Assistance using Misinformation Detection and Explanation") contain the description of the financial variables and ratios used, respectively. Note that the data does not contain any labels regarding whether a FS contains any kind of misinformation or not. This makes using supervised techniques inappropriate. This raw, structured dataset is denoted as Ds​t​rD\_{str}, where each of 2292×5=11,4602292\times 5=11,460 rows consists of 64 (42+22) features for a particular company for a particular year.

Ds​t​rD_{str}

2292×5=11,4602292\times 5=11,460

Audit reports (as text files) are available for each of these companies for all 5 years. We have web-scrapped[6](https://arxiv.org/html/2607.17797v1#footnote6 "footnote 6 ‣ 3 Datasets ‣ Financial Audit Assistance using Misinformation Detection and Explanation") the audit reports of these companies for the same 5-year time span. A company’s financial health and the accuracy of information in its FS are evaluated by the auditors in their audit reports. For the 2292 companies for 5 years, there were a total of 2292×5=114602292\times 5=11460 audit reports. The raw corpus of audit reports is denoted Da​u​dD\_{aud}. After cleaning and removing small and non-sentence lines (e.g., tables), Da​u​dD\_{aud} contains 578789 sentences and 22233701 words. The average number of sentences and words per audit report in the dataset Da​u​dD\_{aud} are 50.50 and 1891.40 respectively. The Figures [2(a)](https://arxiv.org/html/2607.17797v1#S3.F2.sf1 "In Figure 2 ‣ 3 Datasets ‣ Financial Audit Assistance using Misinformation Detection and Explanation") and [2(b)](https://arxiv.org/html/2607.17797v1#S3.F2.sf2 "In Figure 2 ‣ 3 Datasets ‣ Financial Audit Assistance using Misinformation Detection and Explanation") represent the word clouds of nouns and verbs from Da​u​dD\_{aud} respectively.

