XAI aims to provide explanations in various forms, such as weighted or non-weighted subsets of features, rule sets, visual representations, and natural language descriptions. In contrast, the research area of Outlying Aspect Mining (OAM) [SM22], [LBS23] focuses on generating explanations for the anomalousness of a point, typically as a subset of features forming a subspace. While XAI explains the reasoning of an underlying model OAM offers a holistic, model-agnostic view of why a point is interesting or anomalous.

